surname:Repapi;given-names:E</infon><infon key="name_1">surname:Sayers;given-names:I</infon><infon key="name_2">surname:Wain;given-names:LV</infon><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="source">Nat Genet</infon><infon key="type">ref</infon><infon key="year">2009</infon><offset>46998</offset><text>Genome-wide association study identifies five loci associated with lung function.</text></passage><passage><infon key="comment">doi:ng.500 [pii] 10.1038/ng.500</infon><infon key="name_0">surname:Hancock;given-names:DB</infon><infon key="name_1">surname:Eijgelsheim;given-names:M</infon><infon key="name_2">surname:Wilk;given-names:JB</infon><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="source">Nat Genet</infon><infon key="type">ref</infon><infon key="year">2009</infon><offset>47080</offset><text>Meta-analyses of genome-wide association studies identify multiple loci associated with pulmonary function.</text></passage><passage><infon key="fpage">119</infon><infon key="lpage">24</infon><infon key="name_0">surname:Jostins;given-names:L</infon><infon key="name_1">surname:Ripke;given-names:S</infon><infon key="name_2">surname:Weersma;given-names:RK</infon><infon key="pub-id_pmid">23128233</infon><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="source">Nature</infon><infon key="type">ref</infon><infon key="volume">491</infon><infon key="year">2012</infon><offset>47188</offset><text>Host-microbe interactions have shaped the genetic architecture of inflammatory bowel disease.</text></passage><passage><infon key="fpage">25</infon><infon key="lpage">33</infon><infon key="name_0">surname:Deloukas;given-names:P</infon><infon key="name_1">surname:Kanoni;given-names:S</infon><infon key="name_2">surname:Willenborg;given-names:C</infon><infon key="pub-id_pmid">23202125</infon><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="source">Nat Genet</infon><infon key="type">ref</infon><infon key="volume">45</infon><infon key="year">2013</infon><offset>47282</offset><text>Large-scale association analysis identifies new risk loci for coronary artery disease.</text></passage><passage><infon key="fpage">596</infon><infon key="lpage">604</infon><infon key="name_0">surname:Rioux;given-names:JD</infon><infon key="name_1">surname:Xavier;given-names:RJ</infon><infon key="name_2">surname:Taylor;given-names:KD</infon><infon key="pub-id_pmid">17435756</infon><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="source">Nat Genet</infon><infon key="type">ref</infon><infon key="volume">39</infon><infon key="year">2007</infon><offset>47369</offset><text>Genome-wide association study identifies new susceptibility loci for Crohn disease and implicates autophagy in disease pathogenesis.</text></passage><passage><infon key="fpage">744</infon><infon key="lpage">7</infon><infon key="name_0">surname:Stefansson;given-names:H</infon><infon key="name_1">surname:Ophoff;given-names:RA</infon><infon key="name_2">surname:Steinberg;given-names:S</infon><infon key="pub-id_pmid">19571808</infon><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="source">Nature</infon><infon key="type">ref</infon><infon key="volume">460</infon><infon key="year">2009</infon><offset>47502</offset><text>Common variants conferring risk of schizophrenia.</text></passage><passage><infon key="fpage">857</infon><infon key="lpage">64</infon><infon key="name_0">surname:Todd;given-names:JA</infon><infon key="name_1">surname:Walker;given-names:NM</infon><infon key="name_2">surname:Cooper;given-names:JD</infon><infon key="pub-id_pmid">17554260</infon><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="source">Nat Genet</infon><infon key="type">ref</infon><infon key="volume">39</infon><infon key="year">2007</infon><offset>47552</offset><text>Robust associations of four new chromosome regions from genome-wide analyses of type 1 diabetes.</text></passage><passage><infon key="fpage">189</infon><infon key="lpage">97</infon><infon key="name_0">surname:Kathiresan;given-names:S</infon><infon key="name_1">surname:Melander;given-names:O</infon><infon key="name_2">surname:Guiducci;given-names:C</infon><infon key="pub-id_pmid">18193044</infon><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="source">Nat Genet</infon><infon key="type">ref</infon><infon key="volume">40</infon><infon key="year">2008</infon><offset>47649</offset><text>Six new loci associated with blood low-density lipoprotein cholesterol, high-density lipoprotein cholesterol or triglycerides in humans.</text></passage><passage><infon key="fpage">684</infon><infon key="lpage">7</infon><infon key="name_0">surname:Johansen;given-names:CT</infon><infon key="name_1">surname:Wang;given-names:J</infon><infon key="name_2">surname:Lanktree;given-names:MB</infon><infon key="pub-id_pmid">20657596</infon><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="source">Nat Genet</infon><infon key="type">ref</infon><infon key="volume">42</infon><infon key="year">2010</infon><offset>47786</offset><text>Excess of rare variants in genes identified by genome-wide association study of hypertriglyceridemia.</text></passage><passage><infon key="fpage">741</infon><infon key="lpage">50</infon><infon key="name_0">surname:Buist;given-names:AS</infon><infon key="name_1">surname:McBurnie;given-names:MA</infon><infon key="name_2">surname:Vollmer;given-names:WM</infon><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="source">International variation in the prevalence of COPD (the BOLD Study): a
population-based prevalence study</infon><infon key="type">ref</infon><infon key="volume">370</infon><infon key="year">2007</infon><offset>47888</offset></passage><passage><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="type">title_caption</infon><offset>47889</offset><text>Panel – Research in context</text></passage><passage><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="type">paragraph</infon><offset>47919</offset><text>Systematic Review</text></passage><passage><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="type">paragraph</infon><offset>47937</offset><text>The genetic risk factors for COPD are still largely unknown. We searched PubMed with the search terms “genome-wide association” and “COPD” or “airflow”, as well as the genome-wide association study (GWAS) catalog (genome.gov/26525384). At the time of our search, the largest studies to date included approximately 3,500 cases. Evidence from GWAS in other diseases suggests larger sample sizes or analysis of specific subtypes could increase power and identify new genetic determinants of COPD.</text></passage><passage><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="type">paragraph</infon><offset>48443</offset><text>Interpretation</text></passage><passage><infon key="section_type">REF</infon><infon key="type">paragraph</infon><offset>48458</offset><text>Our study in moderate-to-severe and severe COPD confirms genome-wide associations near FAM13A, HHIP, and CHRNA3/CHRNA5/IREB2, and provides evidence in support of new associations near RIN3, MMP12 and TGFB2. GWAS continues to have potential to identify new genetic risk factors that could implicate novel disease mechanisms in COPD. Genetic variants, apart from alpha-1 antitrypsin deficiency, increase the risk of COPD; this burden may be higher in those with severe disease.</text></passage><passage><infon key="file">nihms-582808-f0001.jpg</infon><infon key="id">F1</infon><infon key="section_type">FIG</infon><infon key="type">fig_caption</infon><offset>48934</offset><text>Local association plots for significant loci for the analysis of
moderate-to-severe COPD in COPDGene non-Hispanic whites and African-Americans,
ECLIPSE, NETT/NAS, and GenKOLS (Norway). The x-axis is chromosomal position, and
the y-axis shows the –log10 P-value. The most significant SNP
at each locus is labeled in purple, with other SNPs colored by degree of linkage
disequilibrium (r2).</text></passage><passage><infon key="file">nihms-582808-f0002.jpg</infon><infon key="id">F2</infon><infon key="section_type">FIG</infon><infon key="type">fig_caption</infon><offset>49325</offset><text>Local association plots for significant loci for the analysis of severe COPD in
COPDGene non-Hispanic whites and African-Americans, ECLIPSE, NETT/NAS, and
GenKOLS (Norway). The x-axis is chromosomal position, and the y-axis shows the
– log10 P-value. The most significant SNP at each locus is
labeled in purple, with other SNPs colored by degree of linkage disequilibrium
(r2).</text></passage><passage><infon key="file">T1.xml</infon><infon key="id">T1</infon><infon key="section_type">TABLE</infon><infon key="type">table_caption</infon><offset>49705</offset><text>Baseline characteristics.</text></passage><passage><infon key="file">T1.xml</infon><infon key="id">T1</infon><infon key="section_type">TABLE</infon><infon key="type">table</infon><infon key="xml">&lt;?xml version=&quot;1.0&quot; encoding=&quot;UTF-8&quot;?&gt;
